The world's people: the stand-in for the player's character and for the pedestrians.

Both files are built from MakeHuman assets released under CC0 1.0 Universal
(creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/): dedicated to the public domain, free to use, change
and redistribute for any purpose, commercial or not, with no attribution required. They are credited
here anyway. No person's likeness is in them: every face is MakeHuman's base mesh moved by its own
macro targets (gender, age, weight, muscle, height, proportions), never a scan of anyone.

File(s)                Built from
standin.glb            the player's character: base mesh with five body morphs, hair, beard, glasses
standin_crowd.glb      five pedestrians, two levels of detail each, in one texture atlas

The licence was read on the MakeHuman project's own site, static.makehumancommunity.org:
about/license.html ("All core assets are shared under Creative Commons, CC0") and the asset-pack
pages that list each asset with its licence (assets/assetpacks/<pack>.html). Every asset's own file
says CC0 as well (its .mhclo, .mhmat or .obj header, or the pack's JSON index). The sources' own
pages at makehumancommunity.org/node/<n> did not answer from the machine that built these; the pack
pages that name them did. No checksums are published for the packs; the zips used had these sha256:
  makehuman_system_assets_cc0.zip  b542127a8e25547c7c29c19f2d1d2adb9a664c80396ecd694095dbc8028a0107
  bodyparts05_cc0.zip              262bba42246f85b2a91f493dd920296b258a3b4544eb495c91c4d08e57c528fd
  glasses01_cc0.zip                f215c58e09e31b7ee568c814067cb47704cee6da1f6fc01cffb8e9fca37bafdd
  hair01_cc0.zip                   49445d69848a313ec41a9970f6a0fe4bcf925c9f1c6ef40a76f119c2e07940c9
  mpfb2-20260911.zip (the base mesh, targets, game-engine rig and its weights, all CC0; MPFB's code,
  GPL-3.0, was only run as a tool and is not in these files)

