The makehuman_system assets' copyright holders at their release to CC0 (September 2020) were Data
Collection AB, Joel Palmius and Jonas Hauquier.

What was changed. Each character was made in Blender 4.5 with MPFB 2.0.17 from the assets above
(the macros differ between the hero's variants and the pedestrians), fitted, rigged with the game
engine rig (Unreal Engine bone names) and exported, then put through the world's people pipeline:
skinned to the rest pose, turned to face -Z in metres, bones outside the Unreal Engine body set
folded into their nearest kept parent, a one-piece outfit split into top and bottom by the bones it
moves with, glasses' lenses removed, a shorter "curls" style derived from afro01 by pulling it
towards the scalp, the hero's angular, curved, older, slim and broad bodies added as morph targets,
everything decimated with meshoptimizer, quantised, and every colour map turned into a detail map
(its mean colour normalised) and re-encoded as WebP (hero up to 1024 px, crowd atlas tiles 512 px).
